 K., Krogh, A., McLean, J., Moule, S., Murphy, L., Oliver, K., Osborne, J., Quail, M. A., Rajandream, M. A., Rogers, J., Rutter, S., Seeger, K., Skelton, J., Squares, R., Squares, S., Sulston, J. E., Taylor, K., Whitehead, S., and Barrell, B. G. (<year>1998</year>) <source>Nature</source> <volume>393</volume> <fpage>537</fpage>&#x02013;544<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9634230</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref24"><label>24</label><citation citation-type="journal">Mougous, J. D., Petzold, C. J., Senaratne, R. H., Lee, D. H., Akey, D. L., Lin, F. L., Munchel, S. E., Pratt, M. R., Riley, L. W., Leary, J. A., Berger, J. M., and Bertozzi, C. R. (<year>2004</year>) <source>Nat. Struct. Mol. Biol.</source> <volume>11</volume> <fpage>721</fpage>&#x02013;729<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15258569</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref25"><label>25</label><citation citation-type="journal">Jain, M., and Cox, J. S. (<year>2005</year>) <source>PLoS Pathog.</source> <volume>1</volume> <fpage>e2</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16201014</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref26"><label>26</label><citation citation-type="journal">Six, D. A., Carty, S. M., Guan, Z., and Raetz, C. R. (<year>2008</year>) <source>Biochemistry</source> <volume>47</volume> <fpage>8623</fpage>&#x02013;8637<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18656959</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref27"><label>27</label><citation citation-type="journal">Rohde, K. H., Abramovitch, R. B., and Russell, D. G. (<year>2007</year>) <source>Cell Host Microbe</source> <volume>2</volume> <fpage>352</fpage>&#x02013;364<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18005756</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref28"><label>28</label><citation citation-type="journal">Hampshire, T., Soneji, S., Bacon, J., James, B. W., Hinds, J., Laing, K., Stabler, R. A., Marsh, P. D., and Butcher, P. D. (<year>2004</year>) <source>Tuberculosis</source> <volume>84</volume> <fpage>228</fpage>&#x02013;238<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15207492</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ref29"><label>29</label><citation citation-type="journal">Chesne-Seck, M. L., Barilone, N., Boudou, F., Gonzalo Asensio, J., Kolattukudy, P. E., Martin, C., Cole, S. T., Gicquel, B., Gopaul, D. N., and Jackson, M. (<year>2008</year>) <source>J. Bacteriol.</source> <volume>190</volume> <fpage>1329</fpage>&#x02013;1334<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18065542</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list><fn-group><fn id="fn4"><label>3</label><p>The abbreviations used are: SL-1, sulfolipid-1; PAT, polyacyltrehalose; PCoA, palmitoyl coenzyme A; T2P, trehalose 2-palmitate; T3P, trehalose 3-palmitate; ESI-FT-ICR MS, electrospray ionization Fourier transform ion cyclotron mass spectrometry; MS<italic><sup>n</sup></italic>, linear ion trap tandem mass spectrometry; MBP, maltose-binding protein; DTT, dithiothreitol; TCEP, tris(2-carboxyethyl)phosphine; DMSO, dimethyl sulfoxide; MeOH, methanol; CHCl<sub>3</sub>, chloroform; IPA, isopropyl alcohol.</p></fn></fn-group></back></article>